\import [[$:/plugins/wikilabs/bundler/readme]]

! User Interface

The plugin adds 2 places to work with bundles: the ''Bundle'' tab in the tiddler info area (left) and the ''Bundles'' tab in the right sidebar.

[img[bundler-ui-overview.png]]

!! Right Sidebar: Bundles Tab

The <$button actions=<<rightSidebarBundlesTab>> class="tc-btn-invisible tc-tiddlylink">right sidebar Bundles tab</$button> lists all bundles. It gives you fast access to exports and to the bundle configurations.

* {{$:/core/images/export-button|1em}} ... Export all tiddlers of the bundle
* The drag icon ... Drag it into a different wiki, to import the bundle and all its tiddlers
* The tiddler count ... Click it to preview the list:

|Action |Behaviour |h
|click |Open the bundle configuration in $:/AdvancedSearch |
|CTRL-click |Open all tiddlers in the story river |
|CTRL-SHIFT-click |Open all tiddlers below the current bundle tiddler |

Long lists can be shortened with the filter input at the top of the tab:

[img[bundler-list-filter-input-short.png]]

!! Tiddler Info: Bundle Tab

Open a bundle tiddler and click its {{$:/core/images/info-button|1em}} info button. The ''Bundle'' tab shows:

* The drag link, to copy the bundle into a different wiki
* The export button and the number of tiddlers
* Buttons to test the configuration in the $:/AdvancedSearch ''Filter'' tab, to open the list in the story, or to open it below the bundle tiddler
* The list of all tiddlers in the bundle

[img[new-story-buttons-annotated.png]]

The ''Bundle'' tab can be set as the default info tab in the <$button actions=<<openControlBundlesTab>> class="tc-btn-invisible tc-tiddlylink">Bundler settings</$button>.

!! Settings

The <$button actions=<<openControlBundlesTab>> class="tc-btn-invisible tc-tiddlylink">Bundler settings</$button> let you:

* Choose the position of the sidebar tab
* Show or hide the drag and export buttons in the sidebar
* Enable <<.xL "Filtered Bundles" "doc-filtered-bundles">>
* Enable the <<.xL "import features" "doc-import-workflow">>

[img[new-enable-drag-export-config-settings.png]]

!! Works Well With

* ''$:/AdvancedSearch'' ... <<.xL "Filtered Bundles" "doc-filtered-bundles">> show up in the ''Filter'' tab dropdown, next to the core filters
* ''Relink plugin'' ... Bundle tiddlers use the field `code-body: yes`, so Relink updates titles in bundles when tiddlers are renamed
* ''[[Advanced Search Plus|https://wikilabs.github.io/editions/advanced-search-plus/]]'' ... An improved $:/AdvancedSearch for advanced users and developers
